# Untracked on purpose. lazy.nvim rewrites this on every install and update, and
# ~/.config/nvim is a symlink into the repo — so tracking it means either a
# perpetually dirty repo or a bootstrap dance to stop a first launch on a new
# machine from clobbering the pins. This config is stock LazyVim plus two small
# override files, so installing current plugins is the cheaper trade. See README.
lazy-lock.json

# Below: LazyVim starter defaults.
tt.*
.tests
doc/tags
debug
.repro
foo.*
*.log
data
